WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.529
Welcome to Stanford Graduate School of
Business. Follow our MSx students as they

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:09.900
take you on a 360 degree tour of student
and family residences. We have a breadth

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.820
of on-campus housing options to fit your
family as well as your lifestyle. Our

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.039
first stop is Escondido Village
primarily serving MSx, MBA, and other

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:24.269
graduate student families. Here's Carlos
who lives here with his wife Dora and

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:26.779
their three children.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.300
Hey, good morning. I'm Carlos. I'm an MSx student at the Graduate
School of Business here at Stanford and

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.520
this is my house. We live in Escondido Village, which is five minute bike

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.320
ride to the School of Business and
right now I'm taking my little one to

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:51.149
the daycare. Let's go. Escondido Village
houses more than 4000 graduate students

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.230
and their families. With a vibrant
community of students, partners, and

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:59.219
children, there are numerous nearby
playgrounds and on-campus daycare and

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:03.650
schooling options. Plus it's only a
10-minute walk to the business school.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:09.240
Next, follow Huimin, who lives in Munger
Graduate Residences. Munger offers studios

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.700
and one, two, and four bedroom apartments.
Munger houses 600 graduate students and

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.840
their partners across all disciplines
and graduate schools at Stanford. It's

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.240
contemporary design emphasizes open
common areas, community, and

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.240
cross-disciplinary discussion. Huimin
lives in one of the two bedroom

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.439
apartments. These furnished apartments
offer generous square footage private,

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:35.299
bathrooms, and full sized kitchens.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:43.409
So here we are at my dorm at Munger Residence. What I love about Munger is that we have a
big community of students from many

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:47.520
different schools. Here
we have all sorts of social activities

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:54.780
including tea time, barbecue and movie time. My favorite is tea time. Munger is a short seven minute walk to

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.670
the business school and it's never a bad
walk considering we have 261 days of

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.770
sunshine every year. Even closer are the
GSB residences – they offer individual

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.510
rooms and kitchens shared by two rooms.
Meet Rob who lives at Jack McDonald Hall

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:14.730
which is part of GSB residences. Oh hey
there. I'm Rob, now a part of the MSx

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.530
program here In Jack McDonald Hall. This is a great place to live and it's

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.280
also great to be right across from the
GSB where you get to tap into the

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.270
wonderful MSx and broader GSB
communities. Anyway I got to run right

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:30.990
now and play some pool but I'll catch up
with you guys later. All residences have

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:35.250
communal and social spaces for students
to unwind, connect, and organize

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.690
activities. No matter where you live on
Stanford's campus you'll be part of a

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:44.990
vibrant community and form strong
friendships that will last a lifetime.

